WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Speaker 1: Our friend, Congressman Jamie&nbsp;
Raskin, who's been a guest on this program,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:12.300
says that Donald Trump will likely end his life&nbsp;
behind bars. This I have to see because I have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:19.560
very, very difficult time believing that. Newsweek&nbsp;
reports Trump likely to be indicted will end life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:26.340
quote, behind bars. Congressman says former&nbsp;
President Donald Trump will likely be indicted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:31.500
and spend the rest of his life behind bars.&nbsp;
Representative Jamie Raskin said on Saturday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:37.020
Raskin is a maryland Democrat and served on the&nbsp;
House Select Committee investigating the Capitol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:44.280
riots. The panel spent months probing Trump's role&nbsp;
in the insurrection. Raskin reflected about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:50.160
significance of the report issued by the committee&nbsp;
during an appearance on Yahoo News's Skullduggery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:55.620
podcast Saturday. The Democratic lawmaker said&nbsp;
he, quote, would be really would be surprised if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:00.840
Attorney General Merrick Garland did not indict&nbsp;
Trump for his alleged role in the riot, adding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:06.960
that it's so clear that the president intended&nbsp;
to interfere with the election certification.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:13.740
Raskin went on to say, I do think it's very,&nbsp;
very important that we establish that it's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:21.300
just footsoldiers, but kingpins who are prosecuted&nbsp;
and that it's just wrong to send hundreds of foot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:28.920
soldiers to jail and leave the very clear kingpin&nbsp;
unprosecuted. He added that Trump could spend the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:33.420
rest of his life in prison if he's convicted&nbsp;
on January six charges. There's just deep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:40.320
culpability from the very beginning in everything&nbsp;
that Donald Trump did. I'm very serious about him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:46.320
facing the consequences and paying for the cost&nbsp;
of his action. He could spend the remaining days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:55.440
of his misanthropic life behind bars, presumably&nbsp;
with Secret Service agents. I would love for Jamie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:03.060
Raskin to be correct here. I really would. The&nbsp;
blatant criminality and flouting of the law by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:11.640
Donald Trump is absolutely stunning and appalling.&nbsp;
And we hope that the safeguards we have in place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:17.940
are actually robust and strong enough that they&nbsp;
can hold someone like Donald Trump accountable. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:22.620
would love for Jamie Raskin to be right that that&nbsp;
accountability is going to be prison time. I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:28.560
think that it is. And again, it goes through let's&nbsp;
think through the steps. First step is Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:34.620
Trump has to be indicted. Hasn't happened yet, but&nbsp;
maybe it will. Trump gets indicted. Next step is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:41.460
does it even go to trial? Or is Trump as a former&nbsp;
president who will have the best of the best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:47.640
legal advice going to strike a deal and make a&nbsp;
deal either where he doesn't have to admit to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:56.460
any guilt, but he pays fines or he has to plead&nbsp;
guilty to something minor. And the consequence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:01.320
of jail time, prison time is not even on the&nbsp;
table. If you get beyond that and you say, okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:07.320
he's going to have to go to trial and it's going&nbsp;
to include the possibility of a prison sentence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:15.420
How do you get a jury to fairly evaluate a former&nbsp;
president's actions? I don't know who you can find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:20.460
that wouldn't bring a strong preconceived notion&nbsp;
and preconceived opinion about Trump's guilt or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:25.560
innocence. And by the way, as I've said before,&nbsp;
if you can find people who really have no opinion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.820
I would wonder whether where they've been for&nbsp;
the last six years and whether these are even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:33.660
really the people competent enough to serve on&nbsp;
a jury. Although it's a jury of your peers, I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:40.140
understand everybody gets to serve. So how do you&nbsp;
even put a jury together if you then get a guilty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:46.380
verdict that sticks, that doesn't get appealed?&nbsp;
There may not necessarily be prison time. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:52.980
if there is a guilty verdict and if there is&nbsp;
prison time and Trump gets sentenced, older,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.980 --> 00:04:01.140
wealthy folks close to 80 years old with prison&nbsp;
sentences use every possibility available to them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:08.280
every health issue that they have, and argue&nbsp;
for house arrest instead of actual prison. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:14.820
I believe that if everything went perfectly&nbsp;
indictment, serious charges, conviction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:22.260
sentencing, that even includes prison time. I&nbsp;
think you get a suspended sentence or at the very,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:30.300
very worst for Trump, you get home confinement.&nbsp;
So I know he's Mr. Perfect Health six 3 to 39,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:35.580
healthiest president ever. I assure you that will&nbsp;
be a very different story painted about his health&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:41.820
if all of a sudden prison is on the table. And&nbsp;
I would bet anything that Trump doesn't see a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:48.240
day in a jail or prison cell. If you disagree with&nbsp;
me. I want to hear from you. I just don't see it.

